# Assistant content: a thinking (reasoning) step. internal/tui/
# transcript.go's RenderThinking is only ever committed with
# Expanded: false (internal/tui/app.go's handleThinking never sets it
# true, and the live view at app.go:1778 hardcodes view.Expanded = false
# too), so per its own doc comment ("collapsed... shows nothing") the
# committed block renders as nothing at all, not a folded placeholder —
# there is no on-screen affordance this scenario found that ctrl+o
# expands into the "∴ Thinking" row RenderThinking can otherwise produce.
# The EXPECT_NOT lines below record that as a real behaviour, not a typo:
# if a future change wires Expanded through, these two would start
# failing and that's the signal.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/content-thinking.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE explain the change
KEY enter
WAITFOR /I'll use a fixed window counter/ 20
SHOT reply-collapsed
EXPECT /I'll use a fixed window counter/
EXPECT_NOT /fixed window, not a sliding one/
EXPECT_NOT /∴/
KEY ctrl+o
SHOT after-ctrl-o-expand
EXPECT_NOT /fixed window, not a sliding one/
KEY ctrl+o
SHOT after-ctrl-o-collapse
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
